{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for hosted MCP Draft 2 at exact d69b46ba6b649b257b68ffa12f170212d174d550, primary c7d70269815ea36a24ebe8587a05ec64919a8dc2 FIRST, normally assigned original f88c4944/705999cf. Design review only; no deployed exploit/runtime failure claimed. Draft2 repairs controller/admin authorization, native new-key enrollment, archival, await interleaving, modern header validation and downtime reconciliation. Five P2s remain.\n\n1. Persist pending create before crossing objects (§3.2–3.3,H1/H3). Op/body/final-answer storage cannot recover a registry reset after enrollment accepts but before completion: retry can allocate a different object/key, hit the used invitation and strand the original enrolled key. Concurrent duplicates can allocate twice. Atomically reserve complete request identity/fingerprint and original agent ID/state before any creation/enrollment await. Idempotently resume that exact seed/envelope, read back before native submission, and save recoverable bearer/answer before reply. Specify actor/membership/incarnation/action/target/body conflicts, current-authority replay checks and unfinished-binding retention after expiry. Couple bearer/retire identity+answer with rotation/retirement/session invalidation atomically. Witness resets after reservation, key/envelope persistence, native acceptance before registry completion, and completion before delivery; concurrent retries retain one agent/key/envelope/bearer.\n\n2. Reserve completion space before dispatch (§3.6 Growth/full,H6). The 1GiB write guard conflicts with guaranteed settlement unless outstanding result capacity is reserved. Native settle350–365 appends a receipt/outcome and writes the changed record; send/step can receive results after dispatch while other records fill storage. Rollback preserves an unknown envelope, not its decisive answer. Specify accounting/reservations or durable overflow for serialized records/chunks/segments/in-flight results and separate control/session/config/key budgets. Refuse before sending when required retention cannot be guaranteed. H6 must fill storage with an exact intent outstanding, then retain its accepted result through settlement/reset/readback without replacing its envelope or violating the bound.\n\n3. Partition segments by bytes (§3.6 Records,H6). The existing64 rule limits inline outcome count, not cumulative segment bytes: custody205–218 spills and node260–275 appends to the identity segment. Static peer example:120 explicit refused resubmissions with20KiB names leave64inline/56spilled; names alone exceed1MiB. Continued growth can exceed the platform row limit. This is contract arithmetic, not execution or accepted-terminal resend. Require ordered byte-bounded segment/chunk rows, including oversized single outcomes and metadata, with atomic index/record publication preserving every outcome. Witness large refusals and interrupted spill/reset. Cloudflare bounds whole rows/strings/BLOBs, not just payloads. https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/\n\n4. Separate last-listed from notification state (§3.5,H5). Contrary to the unchanged-Wire claim, watchLegacy121–128 assigns session.told before notification; tools/list also writes it. Persisting every assignment mistakes delivery for a list/receipt; ignoring them loses real lists. Specify durable lastListed and per-stream lastNotified with explicit adapter mapping, or a bounded Wire change/persistence hook. Witness notification without listing, reset/reconnect, then listing/reconnect; old GET closure must not detach its replacement. Fresh-generation reconciliation remains the right repair.\n\n5. Validate legacy version headers (§3.4/H8). Legacy Mcp-* cannot all be ignored: supplied invalid/unsupported MCP-Protocol-Version requires HTTP400. Missing headers may use negotiated session context. Ignore only modern-only mirror headers. Add POST/GET/DELETE valid, absent-with-known-session, invalid and unsupported cases refusing before dispatch. Official primary source: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/blob/main/docs/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports.mdx\n\nAdditional H4/H5/H8 corrections: ParseError/InvalidRequest with undetectable ID requires id:null, not omission; transport exceptions are separate (https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification). Permit required ID correlation without echoing secrets. Apply header safety to raw encoded Mcp-Name, not decoded UTF8; cover Unicode/whitespace sentinel names and malformed encoding. Modern acknowledgments convey honored filter/ID, not a standard replay-retention flag. Distinguish abrupt eviction from graceful retirement, count both stream types under four, and verify rotation closes existing streams/sessions.\n\nP3 fidelity: native membership417–421,679–684 receives and hashes plaintextsecret in enrol's signed fields; admitted native history retains them. Correct digest-only/nowhere-else prose to no additional hosted log/config copies beyond custody/native history. Do not redact/change native bytes to satisfy prose.\n\nArchitecture: object partitioning, dedicated control domain, native enrollment and shared service ports remain suitable once handoff/full-store recovery is specified. Security: current authority/exact binding improves Draft1; isolation does not replace those checks. Simplification: one native enrollment/shared HTTP layer, with durable logical state separate from ephemeral delivery; no stateless fallback or scope cut.\n\nCoverage: Root FIRST direct FULL primary30526B499LF SHA c13f3c99c6e232467987588c9483ad27b3e3903c6036f5250b2ed24585b9a0bd, seven spans/EOF; three peer reports FULL. Framework U344286B FULL; protocol U3 metadata only. Native units directly selected or inherited through actual prior selected coverage/native equality; whole runtime modules PARTIAL. Root separately read current watch/settle/outcome/segment and native secret fields. Official primary web excerpts only, not whole-page FULL. No execution/tests/gate/install/private evidence/provider/browser/deployment/Source edits. H1–H8, once gate, exact implementation review/landing and live recorded check remain prospective. Discovery is predecessor; full Stage2, OAuth, deferred reads/resources/prompts, export and Start-link parser stay owed. Parent34c4 is not silently expanded.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c7d70269815ea36a24ebe8587a05ec64919a8dc2","binding":"assigned","head":"d69b46ba6b649b257b68ffa12f170212d174d550","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:553539414fabbfc1b102371c26bd90fec3f112aa\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:705999cfd6bcb95dfac0f52bd180fd0df3511439\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ecfd66028fdf92748cad56a0e985566de05376b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}